\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Tradeoff of Humanitarian and Economic Costs (as \% of 2019 GDP) for various governmental policies $\bm  {P}$ starting on March 15th and continuing for 3 months. The color indicates the average strength of the restrictions across the 3 months, where 1 represents no action and 7 represents lockdown. The gray bars are heuristic uncertainty bands obtained by combining DELPHI forecast error with bootstrap variation in the rank-$1$ policy-effect estimates. Blue star refers to the actual implemented policy and red diamond refers to the most restrictive policy. Normalizing to \% of GDP enables direct cross-country comparison of relative cost magnitudes.}}{20}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:human_econ_costs_mar15}{{4}{20}{Tradeoff of Humanitarian and Economic Costs (as \% of 2019 GDP) for various governmental policies $\bm {P}$ starting on March 15th and continuing for 3 months. The color indicates the average strength of the restrictions across the 3 months, where 1 represents no action and 7 represents lockdown. The gray bars are heuristic uncertainty bands obtained by combining DELPHI forecast error with bootstrap variation in the rank-$1$ policy-effect estimates. Blue star refers to the actual implemented policy and red diamond refers to the most restrictive policy. Normalizing to \% of GDP enables direct cross-country comparison of relative cost magnitudes}{figure.caption.11}{}}
